WEBVTT

00:00:03.180 --> 00:00:11.980
Intrigue in the Bakumatsu

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:29.840
Tsukikage kooru daichi wo

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:33.670
Korogari fumiwakete yuku

00:00:33.670 --> 00:00:40.880
Horobi to saisei no jidai ga hajimaru

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:44.550
Jiyuu wo omoku kakagete

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:48.120
Michinaki michi wo erande

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:55.230
Mahiru yori mabushii nichibotsu wo koete

00:00:55.230 --> 00:01:02.230
Yume wo kataru you ni toki no fune wa yuku

00:01:02.230 --> 00:01:11.340
Sono yamiji no mukou ni atarashii yoake

00:01:12.110 --> 00:01:19.250
Bokura wa kitto kurayami no kaina kara umarete kita

00:01:19.250 --> 00:01:22.790
Kanawanu koi wo suruyou ni

00:01:22.790 --> 00:01:26.760
Hikari e to samayotteku

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:32.000
Doko made mo hateshino nai kono michi wo

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:37.490
Kaeru sube wa nai

00:02:09.330 --> 00:02:10.600
Vice-Commander Hijikata!

00:02:13.170 --> 00:02:16.810
Kai Shimada

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:16.810
So you've come to Sendai, too!

00:02:14.170 --> 00:02:16.810
Kazue Soma

00:02:17.140 --> 00:02:24.410
Akizuki, until the cause of your negative aura
is revealed, goodbye for now.

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:34.080
Here they come!
They're huge!

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:39.660
"Bring them aboard", you say?

00:02:41.070 --> 00:02:46.770
Comrade Enomoto mentioned that he wants
a kabuki actor who's fit to deal with rough stuff.

00:02:47.870 --> 00:02:50.840
Rough stuff? Kabuki actor?

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:53.510
Someone like Danjuro.

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:57.020
Hey, hey, hold on a second!

00:02:57.020 --> 00:02:58.950
<i>DANJURO</i>
<i>ICHIKAWA</i>

00:03:03.590 --> 00:03:07.350
What is Enomoto doing?
I haven't seen him all day.

00:03:07.990 --> 00:03:10.190
He's locked himself in his room.

00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:14.360
He must be thinking up ideas
for the story's climax.

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:18.600
Don't tell me he's copying the script you wrote!

00:03:18.770 --> 00:03:20.030
Hardly likely.

00:03:21.110 --> 00:03:23.300
Still, you'll find out soon enough.

00:03:37.190 --> 00:03:39.120
<i>To Kazunari Sainen</i>

00:03:45.460 --> 00:03:51.440
Lord Shoten and I have known each other
and we both share a love of food.

00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:58.110
This is a request from him, so no problem.
Feel free to stay at my temple for a while.

00:03:58.110 --> 00:04:03.410
Well, actually I should say that
I'm more into women than food.

00:04:12.460 --> 00:04:15.390
Feel free to use this space.

00:04:15.390 --> 00:04:18.360
So, you two are...

00:04:21.670 --> 00:04:23.930
Did you two fight or something?

00:04:24.600 --> 00:04:27.700
All right, let me handle that for you!

00:04:28.510 --> 00:04:31.100
Aoba Castle

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:43.120
Vice-Commander!

00:04:43.890 --> 00:04:45.050
Vice-Commander Hijikata!

00:04:46.590 --> 00:04:49.460
Vice-Commander! We've been waiting for you!

00:04:50.260 --> 00:04:51.390
Hijikata-sensei!

00:04:55.430 --> 00:04:58.200
It is the beginning of the ninth month
of the fourth year of the Keio Era.

00:04:58.670 --> 00:05:06.770
Toshizo Hijikata enters Sendai, and attends
a war council with the Ou Alliance at Aoba Castle.

00:05:07.310 --> 00:05:13.590
However, many of the provinces in the alliance have
buckled under the New Government Army's attack,

00:05:13.590 --> 00:05:16.860
or have left the alliance to sue for peace.

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:20.450
Sendai Province's Leader Yoshikuni Date

00:05:16.860 --> 00:05:20.450
The alliance is on the verge of collapse.

00:05:21.690 --> 00:05:27.070
Nagaoka fell, and both Yonezawa and Aizu
are about to surrender.

00:05:27.070 --> 00:05:30.800
The outcome of this war is quite obvious.

00:05:31.140 --> 00:05:34.740
Continuing to fight any longer
is tantamount to dying for nothing.

00:05:34.740 --> 00:05:36.140
Exactly!

00:05:38.540 --> 00:05:43.680
If that's the case, we should consider
the future of our citizens...

00:05:43.680 --> 00:05:44.940
Here's my opinion!
If that's the case, we should consider
the future of our citizens...

00:05:45.650 --> 00:05:50.620
I think our best option is to humbly
prostrate ourselves before them

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:55.720
and hope they'll be gracious enough
to extend us mercy.

00:05:55.960 --> 00:05:58.530
I agree with him!

00:05:58.530 --> 00:05:59.560
He's right!

00:05:59.560 --> 00:06:03.270
Then why don't we humbly-

00:06:03.270 --> 00:06:05.740
Why don't we go out there and die with pride?

00:06:08.110 --> 00:06:11.670
I don't see anything pointless
in samurai dying in battle!

00:06:12.380 --> 00:06:16.710
This is nonsense! First of all,
this is no time for such talk!

00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:21.210
Superbly done, Hijikata-san.

00:06:22.890 --> 00:06:24.680
Tell me your name.

00:06:26.190 --> 00:06:28.090
I'm Sotetsu Ibaragi.

00:06:28.890 --> 00:06:32.520
I'm here as representative
of my comrade Enomoto.

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:36.530
"Representative"? What happened to Enomoto?

00:06:36.530 --> 00:06:41.030
My comrade Enomoto has decided to
stay on his ship for various reasons.

00:06:41.470 --> 00:06:46.500
Don't tell me even Fleet Commander
Enomoto is scared?

00:06:54.620 --> 00:06:56.020
What an insult!

00:06:56.020 --> 00:06:58.220
Who does he think we are?

00:06:58.220 --> 00:06:59.950
He's nothing but some upstart!

00:07:03.130 --> 00:07:05.720
So he's the one fit to deal with this rough stuff?

00:07:08.930 --> 00:07:13.730
I'd expect nothing less from a leader of
the Shinsengumi... Toshizo Hijikata.

00:07:30.120 --> 00:07:32.560
So you're worried about him?

00:07:32.790 --> 00:07:34.260
No, nothing like that.

00:07:34.490 --> 00:07:40.260
Come on, take this with you.
I'm sure you'll get hungry.

00:07:40.930 --> 00:07:43.200
I'll do the cleaning.

00:07:44.200 --> 00:07:45.140
B-but...

00:07:45.140 --> 00:07:48.610
Oh, so you two don't have
that type of relationship yet?

00:07:48.610 --> 00:07:51.130
Then you really need to go see him.

00:07:51.240 --> 00:07:52.110
Here.

00:07:54.280 --> 00:07:56.980
Just go, go.

00:08:02.350 --> 00:08:03.910
Thank you!

00:08:07.690 --> 00:08:11.490
Ah, youth!

00:08:41.890 --> 00:08:43.420
Akizuki-sama...

00:08:55.810 --> 00:08:57.300
It's beautiful.

00:09:25.870 --> 00:09:28.070
So you think you can handle this?

00:09:28.370 --> 00:09:32.000
One target versus the four of us.
It's more than enough.

00:09:33.580 --> 00:09:35.240
That's encouraging to hear.

00:09:35.780 --> 00:09:39.580
We won't do anything to
trouble you, Commander.

00:09:40.080 --> 00:09:45.040
You just sit back and watch us work from here.

00:09:51.330 --> 00:09:52.520
Very well.

00:10:08.310 --> 00:10:09.870
What are you trying to say?

00:10:10.350 --> 00:10:13.820
Do you mean to tell me you don't
trust what Enomoto said?!

00:10:13.820 --> 00:10:20.450
I'd love to trust him, but he's already
lost two ships to that stormy weather!

00:10:20.560 --> 00:10:23.650
What makes you think we'll even be good
enough to go up against Satsuma and Choshu?

00:10:23.760 --> 00:10:25.200
Nonsense!

00:10:25.200 --> 00:10:28.600
With our Kaiyomaru, the most powerful ship
of the shogunate government,

00:10:28.600 --> 00:10:30.690
the Satsuma-Choshu Forces are nothing to fear!

00:10:30.840 --> 00:10:33.340
But the man who's supposed to be at the helm

00:10:33.340 --> 00:10:36.310
has locked himself in his cabin
and hasn't come out at all!

00:10:36.310 --> 00:10:39.800
We've come to Sendai but he still
hasn't given us any guidance!

00:10:39.940 --> 00:10:41.480
What in the world could we even fight
against in this kind of condition?

00:10:41.480 --> 00:10:42.680
How dare you?

00:10:42.680 --> 00:10:46.450
It seems that another heated war council
is being held here as well.

00:11:21.320 --> 00:11:22.980
You and I shouldn't be...

00:11:26.320 --> 00:11:28.380
Would you please stay away from me?

00:11:29.490 --> 00:11:32.560
I don't want you caught up in this, Leader.

00:11:32.560 --> 00:11:35.560
I've already become caught up in it.

00:11:36.170 --> 00:11:39.000
I'm sorry, but we shouldn't travel
the same path together.

00:11:40.240 --> 00:11:42.070
Is that right?

00:11:42.070 --> 00:11:48.170
Your sword... Look at how it's made...
It's exactly like the one I picked up.

00:11:50.110 --> 00:11:54.020
Toshogu is where the Head of the Conqueror
used to be sealed away.

00:11:55.120 --> 00:11:57.710
It's not surprising that they're the same swords.

00:11:59.060 --> 00:12:02.490
But that sword chose me!

00:12:04.060 --> 00:12:05.150
That's what you want to believe.

00:12:11.840 --> 00:12:19.310
Hitotsu, higure ni gan kakete
One, make a wish on a sunset

00:12:19.310 --> 00:12:24.280
Futatsu, fudasho no tsukimi-
Two, the primrose at the temp-

00:12:24.280 --> 00:12:25.650
Stop it.

00:12:26.280 --> 00:12:29.390
I've been thinking about it for a long time.

00:12:29.390 --> 00:12:33.760
Akizuki-sama, you knew this song, too!

00:12:36.130 --> 00:12:40.090
Oryo told me something...

00:12:41.930 --> 00:12:48.400
I don't know why, but I can smell
the same thing from you and Yo...

00:12:49.910 --> 00:12:57.350
That's right! Ever since we met in Yokohama,
you and I have been on the same path...

00:12:57.350 --> 00:12:58.250
Say no more!

00:12:59.650 --> 00:13:00.780
Akizuki-sama...

00:13:01.820 --> 00:13:03.050
Just leave.

00:13:19.940 --> 00:13:20.900
Thank you for fighting with me, sir!

00:13:31.720 --> 00:13:31.850
I'm not done yet!

00:13:31.850 --> 00:13:35.080
Hijikata-sensei looks best when he's doing this.
I'm not done yet!

00:13:35.350 --> 00:13:38.460
Yeah, this reminds me of the time in Kyoto.

00:13:38.460 --> 00:13:39.860
Indeed.

00:13:39.860 --> 00:13:41.960
Compared to how they were in Fushimi,
their morale has improved greatly.

00:13:41.960 --> 00:13:43.260
Thank you for fighting with me, sir!
Compared to how they were in Fushimi,
their morale has improved greatly.

00:13:43.260 --> 00:13:45.130
Compared to how they were in Fushimi,
their morale has improved greatly.

00:13:45.360 --> 00:13:47.630
We wouldn't be here if it
weren't for Hijikata-sensei.

00:13:47.630 --> 00:13:48.600
Exactly.

00:13:52.240 --> 00:13:56.370
On the other hand,
those cowards in the Alliance...

00:13:56.370 --> 00:14:00.310
They might call it a war council,
but all they do is to talk of surrender.

00:14:00.310 --> 00:14:05.940
I've heard that Enomoto's fleet
hasn't even landed in Sendai yet.

00:14:07.690 --> 00:14:10.980
I'm sure he's reached the limits
of his patience, too.

00:14:13.620 --> 00:14:14.680
Why?

00:14:18.860 --> 00:14:20.660
Splendidly done, Hijikata.

00:14:26.100 --> 00:14:28.040
Why does it bother me so much?

00:14:29.040 --> 00:14:30.630
Sotetsu Ibaragi...

00:14:37.650 --> 00:14:38.670
I'm coming in.

00:14:42.250 --> 00:14:43.520
What's that?

00:14:48.430 --> 00:14:55.200
This is still unofficial, but these are the ones
who offered to come aboard our ship.

00:14:55.200 --> 00:14:59.400
However, we still don't have the most
important man of all... our Danjuro...

00:14:59.870 --> 00:15:04.830
People in Sendai have been talking about
surrendering to the New Government.

00:15:05.240 --> 00:15:07.300
We don't have time to be sitting back!

00:15:08.750 --> 00:15:10.480
What is Enomoto saying about this?

00:15:11.520 --> 00:15:13.380
He said, "Just as I speculated".

00:15:14.120 --> 00:15:15.590
How so?

00:15:15.720 --> 00:15:16.580
Who knows.

00:16:02.770 --> 00:16:03.890
Oh?

00:16:11.310 --> 00:16:12.380
What?

00:16:12.380 --> 00:16:13.310
Don't tell me...

00:16:13.810 --> 00:16:15.570
Kakunojo-dono!

00:16:21.350 --> 00:16:22.610
D-don't rush into it!

00:16:26.160 --> 00:16:27.250
Akizuki-sama!

00:16:29.130 --> 00:16:30.750
Please have a match with me!

00:16:36.000 --> 00:16:38.970
We've got a visitor for you.

00:16:43.070 --> 00:16:46.130
I figured you would be showing up soon.

00:16:46.340 --> 00:16:50.340
Tell me... You were laughing
at the war council earlier, weren't you?

00:16:50.850 --> 00:16:54.150
And you were angry.

00:16:54.690 --> 00:17:00.620
Were you laughing at those cowardly men,
thinking that a pack of curs can never win a war?

00:17:01.390 --> 00:17:07.520
With this, the most powerful fleet,
and with you, Hijikata, we can win this war.

00:17:08.130 --> 00:17:10.400
You mean we can save the Tokugawa?

00:17:10.770 --> 00:17:15.470
Saving the Tokugawa... Is that your war?

00:17:15.710 --> 00:17:16.940
That's right.

00:17:16.940 --> 00:17:21.640
I am samurai. I'll stake my life
for the master I serve!

00:17:23.980 --> 00:17:27.440
The Tokugawa will fall.

00:17:37.460 --> 00:17:41.400
I'm certain there are things you will
come to understand if we cross swords.

00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:47.060
I have the same destiny as you, Akizuki-sama.

00:18:06.890 --> 00:18:10.690
The Tokugawa will surely fall.

00:18:11.300 --> 00:18:13.730
However, we are...

00:18:28.980 --> 00:18:30.740
Akizuki-sama...

00:18:48.070 --> 00:18:49.620
Enomoto!

00:19:03.010 --> 00:19:04.240
Enomoto...

00:19:06.820 --> 00:19:08.050
Akizuki-sama!

00:19:17.960 --> 00:19:20.560
It's still bitter, Lord Shoten.

00:19:22.430 --> 00:19:25.430
We got a letter from Yojiro.

00:19:25.670 --> 00:19:26.760
Oh!

00:19:29.210 --> 00:19:35.170
I successfully investigated
Toshogu the other day.

00:19:35.950 --> 00:19:44.150
I found a sword there. My traveling companion
picked it up and hasn't let go since.

00:19:44.890 --> 00:19:48.190
The details of the sword look just
like those on Moontear...

00:19:48.990 --> 00:19:50.390
This is bad.

00:19:50.690 --> 00:19:52.420
I told you it's not ripe yet.

00:19:52.960 --> 00:19:54.450
No...

00:19:55.830 --> 00:19:58.060
I'm not talking about the persimmon.

00:20:19.260 --> 00:20:20.250
Isn't that?

00:20:20.390 --> 00:20:21.980
My comrade Enomoto.

00:20:22.530 --> 00:20:23.860
Enomoto?

00:20:24.760 --> 00:20:31.290
That was very considerate of him.
It was a salute to welcome you.

00:20:37.640 --> 00:20:41.170
I need you to sign your name.

00:20:45.480 --> 00:20:50.580
After the Tokugawa are gone,
how will you be able to fight?

00:20:51.390 --> 00:20:57.090
You once fought for Commander Kondo
and the Shinsengumi.

00:20:54.590 --> 00:20:57.090
Shinsengumi

00:20:57.760 --> 00:21:01.390
You've been fighting for the Tokugawa
ever since Commander Kondo died.

00:21:01.800 --> 00:21:06.860
Now the Tokugawa are about to fall.
What are you going to do?

00:21:07.940 --> 00:21:13.880
But as long as you have a master to serve,
you can still continue to fight as samurai.

00:21:13.880 --> 00:21:16.940
You aren't meant to die in this war.

00:21:17.310 --> 00:21:21.010
I want to see you shine on stage for me.

00:21:21.450 --> 00:21:25.790
I knew it... You're no ordinary playwright...

00:21:58.390 --> 00:22:02.350
<i>UNNECESSARY</i>
<i>DELIBERATION</i>

00:22:03.560 --> 00:22:09.330
Sono te wa ai no tsurugi

00:22:09.330 --> 00:22:18.370
Subete no hajimari no akashi

00:22:19.140 --> 00:22:25.100
Hikaru sora no hate

00:22:25.550 --> 00:22:30.320
Yume wa mada maboroshi

00:22:31.460 --> 00:22:34.560
Tsuki no akari kage ouyouni hashiru kono michi

00:22:34.560 --> 00:22:42.070
Tsuki no akari kage ouyouni hashiru kono michi

00:22:42.070 --> 00:22:47.840
Chigireta ai no tsurugi

00:22:47.840 --> 00:23:00.080
Sashidasu saki wa ikusen no namida ga hitotsu ni nari

00:23:00.080 --> 00:23:05.890
Ashita wo kagayakaseru

00:23:05.890 --> 00:23:11.600
Kono te wa ai no tsurugi

00:23:11.600 --> 00:23:20.300
Subete no hajimari no akashi

00:23:32.970 --> 00:23:47.900
EPISODE 18
PATHETIC
DESTINY

00:23:35.190 --> 00:23:37.790
I shall seal the Head of the Conqueror!

00:23:42.190 --> 00:23:44.260
L-Leader?

00:23:44.260 --> 00:23:46.560
Akizuki-sama!

00:23:47.360 --> 00:23:48.770
Why?

00:23:47.900 --> 00:24:02.570
PATHETIC
DESTINY

00:23:49.030 --> 00:23:51.840
I see, that's how it is.

00:23:52.040 --> 00:23:54.740
O Pitiable Eternal Assassin.

00:23:55.140 --> 00:24:01.410
Because you don't know your own destiny,
you let destiny kill you.
